From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:48:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tderandr: apply a hotplug rule only when all its conditions
 hold

applyHotplugRules() scored each rule by how many of its outputs were in
the requested state and applied the highest score, without requiring
the rest to hold. So a rule that is false still wins whenever nothing
scores higher:

- a single "docked" rule {internal connected, external connected} is
  applied after the external display is unplugged, since the internal
  output alone scores 1;
- a "laptop" rule {internal connected} whose one condition holds loses
  to a "docked" rule {internal connected, external connected, other
  disconnected} with one false condition, which scores 2.

Apply a rule only when every output it names is in the state it asks
for, and among those prefer the rule naming the most outputs, as
before. An output that is not present at all counts as disconnected.
Rules covering every combination, the case the score was built for,
choose exactly as they did.

Measured with tdeinit_displayconfig on an Xorg dummy-driver server
(DUMMY0 connected, DUMMY1 disconnected): before, both cases above
applied the docked profile; after, the first applies nothing and the
second the laptop profile. A rule that fully holds, a rule that does
not hold at all, and a complete laptop/docked pair with the second
output connected behave the same before and after.
---
 tderandr/libtderandr.cpp | 41 ++++++++++++++++++++++------------------
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tderandr/libtderandr.cpp b/tderandr/libtderandr.cpp
index 94828e434..1a96c818e 100644
--- a/tderandr/libtderandr.cpp
+++ b/tderandr/libtderandr.cpp
@@ -1057,31 +1057,36 @@ void KRandrSimpleAPI::applyHotplugRules(TQString kde_confdir) {
 	SingleScreenData *screendata = NULL;
 	HotPlugRulesList::Iterator it;
 	for (it=rules.begin(); it != rules.end(); ++it) {
-		// Compare each rule against the current display configuration
-		// It an output matches the state given in the rule, increment matchCount
+		// A rule applies only if every output it names is in the state the
+		// rule asks for. Among the rules that apply, the one naming the most
+		// outputs is the most specific and wins. Counting matching outputs
+		// alone would let a rule with a false condition win, e.g. a "docked"
+		// rule being applied after the external display was unplugged.
+		// An output that is not present at all counts as disconnected.
 		HotPlugRule rule = *it;
+		int conditionCount = 0;
 		int matchCount = 0;
 		int numberOfScreens = screenInfoArray.count();
-		for (i=0;i<numberOfScreens;i++) {
-			screendata = screenInfoArray.at(i);
-			for (j=0; j<(*it).outputs.count(); j++) {
-				if ((*it).outputs[j] != screendata->screenUniqueName) {
-					continue;
-				}
-				if ((*it).states[j] == HotPlugRule::Connected) {
-					if (screendata->screen_connected) {
-						matchCount++;
-					}
-				}
-				else if ((*it).states[j] == HotPlugRule::Disconnected) {
-					if (!screendata->screen_connected) {
-						matchCount++;
-					}
+		for (j=0; j<(*it).outputs.count() && j<(*it).states.count(); j++) {
+			int state = (*it).states[j];
+			if (state != HotPlugRule::Connected && state != HotPlugRule::Disconnected) {
+				continue;
+			}
+			conditionCount++;
+			bool connected = false;
+			for (i=0;i<numberOfScreens;i++) {
+				screendata = screenInfoArray.at(i);
+				if ((*it).outputs[j] == screendata->screenUniqueName) {
+					connected = screendata->screen_connected;
+					break;
 				}
 			}
+			if (connected == (state == HotPlugRule::Connected)) {
+				matchCount++;
+			}
 		}
 
-		if (matchCount > bestRuleMatchCount) {
+		if (matchCount == conditionCount && matchCount > bestRuleMatchCount) {
 			bestRuleMatchCount = matchCount;
 			bestRule = rule.profileName;
 		}
